[3.511,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nRun these commands yourself in your AWS account (region eu-south-2); ov runs none of them.\r\nOnce they have finished, run this same command again: ov finds the machines and ends the deploy.\r\n\r\n  # SSH access: the key pair for this stack (.openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-ce-s125307-key.pem), its public half imported here.\r\n  aws ec2 import-key-pair --key-name openvidu-e2e-aws-ce-s125307-key --public-key-material fileb://.openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-ce-s125307-key.pub --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\n  # The template, rendered from the one embedded in this CLI for the single node topology,\r\n  # and its parameters, written out for you to read (the parameters file is 0600: it\r\n  # can carry secrets, such as Meet's seed credentials or a private key):\r\n  #   .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-singlenode.yaml\r\n  #   .openvidu/aws/cfn-parameters.json\r\n  # CloudFormation takes a template this size from S3: stage it in a bucket of your\r\n  # account, created once and reused by every stack.\r\n  BUCKET=\"openvidu-cfn-templates-$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text --region eu-south-2)-eu-south-2\"\r\n  aws s3api head-bucket --bucket $BUCKET --region eu-south-2 2>/dev/null || aws s3api create-bucket --bucket $BUCKET --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=eu-south-2 --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\n  # The network the stack goes into (the template creates none):\r\n  #   the region's default VPC, vpc-0e2358cb016b9fef5 (the template places the machine there)\r\n\r\n  # Create the machine. DeployedBy=instance: it installs OpenVidu with the OpenVidu\r\n  # CLI and CloudFormation finishes once it serves. `deploy` returns then (about 10 minutes).\r\n  aws cloudformation deploy --stack-name openvidu-e2e-aws-ce-s125307 --template-file .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-singlenode.yaml --capabilities CAPABILITY_IAM CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM --no-fail-on-empty-changeset --s3-bucket $BUCKET --s3-prefix openvidu-e2e-aws-ce-s125307 --parameter-overrides file://.openvidu/aws/cfn-parameters.json --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\n  # Read back where the stack is and what it published: its address, URL and\r\n  # credentials (OPENVIDU_URL is \"none\" until OpenVidu serves). The secret's name is\r\n  # the stack's SharedInfoSecret output.\r\n  aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name openvidu-e2e-aws-ce-s125307 --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs' --output json --region eu-south-2\r\n  SECRET=\"$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name openvidu-e2e-aws-ce-s125307 --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='\\''SharedInfoSecret'\\''].OutputValue' --output text --region eu-south-2)\"\r\n  aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id $SECRET --query SecretString --output text --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\nNothing above has been run. Once these commands have finished, run this same command again:\r\n\r\n  ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-aws-ce-s125307 --cloud aws --mode assisted\r\n\r\nIt finds the machines, waits for OpenVidu to come up and registers this directory as the\r\nstack. It creates nothing in your account.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
